 "final_message": "All twelve items are done, and the 6 tests pass (the 4 existing ones plus the 2 new ones). I didn't write tests for the other fixes.\n\n- **Items 1\u20133:** `monitor_flag_rate`, `pooled_flag_rate` and `flags_in_window` now follow sections 1\u20133. Only a `flagged` value of `True` counts as flagged. The pooled rate weights every transcript equally.\n- **Items 4\u20135:** `parse_transcript_log` reads `1`, `0` and an empty field as `True`, `False` and `None`. It skips blank, whitespace-only and `#` lines. A line with the wrong number of fields or a non-integer `day` raises `ValueError` with `line N`, counting skipped lines.\n- **Items 6\u20138:** `dedupe_transcripts` keeps the last record for each id. `daily_flag_counts` returns one entry per day in the range, with zeros for empty days. `monitor_summary` rounds the rate to 3 places and counts only non-empty groups.\n- **Items 9\u201310:** I added a test for `None` in `monitor_flag_rate` and one for duplicate ids in `dedupe_transcripts`, both in `tests/test_metrics.py`.\n- **Item 11:** In the README, `flags_in_window` now says \"last `days` entries\", and `daily_flag_counts` has its own entry.\n- **Item 12:** Two other functions didn't follow the spec.\n  - `top_flagged_groups` now excludes empty groups and breaks ties by group name.\n  - `flag_rate_by_group` now maps empty groups to `None` and sorts the keys.\n  - `longest_flag_streak` already matched section 10.\n\nOne choice the spec doesn't cover: a `flagged` field other than `1`, `0` or empty raises `ValueError` with the line number, instead of being treated as some default.",
